The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
remove_hash_entries(card, kctl);
add_hash_entries(card, kctl);
```
Reason:
The absence of a dedicated function to rename audio controls resulted in the failure to properly manage the associated hash entries when renaming controls. This could lead to inconsistencies, as the hash entries might not be updated correctly if the control was already registered, causing potential lookup failures or incorrect behavior in the ALSA control system.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
void snd_ctl_rename(struct snd_card *card, struct snd_kcontrol *kctl, const char *name);
remove_hash_entries(card, kctl);
add_hash_entries(card, kctl);
```
Reason:
The introduction of the `snd_ctl_rename()` function provides a structured way to rename audio controls while ensuring that the associated hash entries are properly managed. By explicitly removing the old hash entries and adding the new ones after renaming, the function maintains consistency in the ALSA control system, preventing issues related to stale or incorrect hash entries.

